---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: SITE.author.name,
    jobTitle: SITE.author.role,
    url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href,
  },
};
---
<Base title="About" description={`About ${SITE.name}: who builds the calculators and how they work.`} schema={schema}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">About {SITE.name}</span></nav>
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Free calculators for Australian homeowners, DIYers and tradies planning building,
        renovation and plumbing work.
      </p>
    
      <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
      <!-- REVISAR: confirma que todo esto es exacto antes de publicar. Puedes añadir una foto y tu LinkedIn. -->
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is built by {SITE.author.name}, a software engineering student who also works on
        residential hydraulic and sanitary design, modelling water supply and drainage systems for
        houses in Revit. He works day to day with Australian trade businesses, including plumbing
        and hydraulics companies, on their websites and systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        That combination is the reason for this site: the maths behind a slab, a tiling job or a hot
        water system is straightforward, but it's often buried in forums or sales pages. These tools
        put it in one place, with the working shown.
      </p>
    
      <h2>How the calculators work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every result shows the formula used, so you can check it.</li>
        <li>Defaults reflect common Australian sizes and practices, and every input can be changed.</li>
        <li>Your inputs are processed in your browser and are not stored.</li>
        <li>Pages are reviewed and updated; each one shows the date it was last updated.</li>
      </ul>
    
      <h2>Accuracy and safety</h2>
      <p>
        Results are estimates to help you plan and compare quotes. They are not a substitute for
        advice from a licensed tradesperson or engineer, and structural, plumbing, gas and electrical
        work in Australia must be done by licensed professionals.
      </p>
    
      <p>Spotted an error or want a new calculator? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
